---
// The three ways to run Remit, as three columns. Same protections in all three.
---
<div class="ways">
	<div class="way">
		<span class="way-k">01</span>
		<h3>Standalone</h3>
		<p class="way-price">Free</p>
		<p>One person, one machine. The coworkers built in and any you write. The machine is its own authority.</p>
		<ul><li>Every protection</li><li>Any model provider</li><li>All connectors and MCP</li><li>No account</li></ul>
	</div>
	<div class="way">
		<span class="way-k">02</span>
		<h3>With your team's gallery</h3>
		<p class="way-price">Free</p>
		<p>The self-hosted broker on your network: sign-in, a shared catalogue of coworkers, uploads reviewed by a person before they are published.</p>
		<ul><li>Everything in Standalone</li><li>Shared coworkers</li><li>Review before publish</li><li>Runs on your server</li></ul>
	</div>
	<div class="way lead">
		<span class="way-k">03</span>
		<h3>Under your organisation's policy</h3>
		<p class="way-price">Remit Cloud Enterprise · US$200 a year</p>
		<p>One signed policy across every machine, a content-free evidence record, a private gallery with a scan on every submission, a fleet inventory and a console.</p>
		<ul><li>Everything in the first two</li><li>Policy that only tightens</li><li>Evidence an auditor can use</li><li>Your identity provider, SCIM</li></ul>
	</div>
</div>
